					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/madman-with-keyboard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1616776); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1616776&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606595993" alt="Madman with Keyboard" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1616776)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/madman-with-keyboard" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1616776); return false;" >Madman with Keyboard</a></span> <span class="odate time_1508813874 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Oct 2017 02:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3618792">
									

<p>I’m torn here. On one hand, this does have a nice sense of humour to it, and that final little note is a nice little ‘oomph’ as it were—and honestly, I do like in a twisted how the SCP Foundation is on speaking terms and generally friendly relations with <em>literally Hell itself</em>.</p>
<p>On the other hand though, it feels a bit <em>too</em> silly, at least for a Mainline article. Like, this has all the kind if set up I feel would make for a good Tale or so, but some part of me—maybe some ancient part that still insists that the SCP is a “Seriosus business of Horror and Inexplicable Spooky stuff”—can’t come to grips with this.</p>
<p>I may change this opinion in the future, but for now, I’m begrudgingly staying Neutral on this. It’s good, but it feels just too Silly—a good kind of Silly, but one I’m torn on supporting. Goos job all the same, however.</p>

							</div>

								
					
