			<div class="content" id="post-content-3619145">
									

<p>Ngl I really don’t like when people say stuff like “I would have upvoted if it was a J” because that kinda misses the point. Articles on this site are about the writing, and if that writing entertained or impressed you. The arbitrary classification of an article itself shouldn’t matter for the most part. If you thought this wasn’t funny or wasn’t good, by all means downvote. I’m well aware my comedic style is divisive to say the least. But if you liked the article, if you laughed, evaluate it for what it is rather than if it has a -J next to its title. Trying to restrict all humorous writing to Js just limits creativity.</p>

